 "description": "<p><strong>Greenland GNSS Network (GNET)</strong></p><p>60 GNSS stations are located along the Greenland ice sheet. Together the stations constitute the Greenland GNSS Network (GNET) and are operated by DTU Space.</p><p>The stations measure elevation changes in Greenland's crust that can be seen as an expression of the ice sheet's mass becomes larger or smaller.</p><p>The measurements from GNET stations makes it possible to follow the variations in the earth's crust over a period of several years and thus it is possible to determine whether there is a net ice cap loss.</p>",
